.KEY VER/A
.BRA {
.KET }
;
; Build an AmiBinkD release archive for the file section.
;
;   Execute DH4:MakeAmiBinkD 10_32
;
; MUST RUN ON THE AMIGA. The Linux host's `lha' is Lhasa, which only
; EXTRACTS. Every release since v9 carries the [Amiga] OS byte, so it is
; built with DH0:C/lha to stay consistent.
;
; Expected layout, matching every release since v10.18:
;     AmiBinkD/  (binary, readme.txt, manual.txt, AmiBinkD-example.cfg,
;                 AmiBinkD.scr, AmiBinkD.info)
;     File_ID.DIZ
;
; 2026-08-21: a build came out FLAT -- all seven files at the archive root,
; no AmiBinkD drawer -- from an lha line byte-identical to the one that
; produced the v10.25 archive correctly. The current directory is the only
; input this script does not control, so it now prints it before archiving
; and lists the result afterwards. If the listing shows no "AmiBinkD/"
; prefix, the Where line above it says what the directory actually was.
;
CD DH4:
Echo "Where (must be DH4:):"
CD
Echo ""
Echo "Drawer contents (must be exactly 6 files, no .PRE_ or .BACKUP):"
List DH4:AmiBinkD LFORMAT="  %N"
Echo ""
Delete UDBase0:NETWORKING/AmiBinkD{VER}.lha QUIET
lha -r a UDBase0:NETWORKING/AmiBinkD{VER}.lha AmiBinkD File_ID.DIZ
Echo ""
Echo "Archive contents (each entry should start AmiBinkD/ except File_ID.DIZ):"
lha l UDBase0:NETWORKING/AmiBinkD{VER}.lha
